WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.740
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit 6:
Sports, Olympics, and Achievement.

2
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.840
Welcome to Unit 6!

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.520
This unit is all about sports, the Olympics,
and what it means to achieve something great.

4
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:17.740
You will explore how athletes train, how
the Olympic Games began in ancient Greece,

5
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.560
and how the Paralympics have changed our
understanding of what the human body can do.

6
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.440
Along the way you will build powerful
vocabulary, strengthen your grammar,

7
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.880
and learn to write about sports with confidence and skill.

8
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:36.420
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:43.860
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read and
understand non-fiction texts about sports and the olympic games.

10
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:50.640
you will also use important vocabulary such as
analogy, bias, evidence, viewpoint, and more.

11
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.920
you will also recognise and form compound nouns (e.g.

12
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.710
football, swimming pool, team-mate).

13
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.460
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:09.980
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: analogy,
argumentative, bias, evidence, objective, viewpoint.

15
00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:16.360
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:20.240
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:28.100
The reading sequence includes Sports, Olympics, and
Achievement: source text 1 and Sports, Olympics, and Achievement:

18
00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:29.750
source text 2.

19
00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:31.080
Read actively.

20
00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:36.260
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

21
00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.460
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

22
00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.840
The first language focus is Compound Nouns.

23
00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.180
What is a compound noun?

24
00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:53.860
A compound noun is made by combining two or more
words to create a new noun with a specific meaning.

25
00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:00.740
Understanding compound nouns helps you express
yourself precisely and makes your writing richer.

26
00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:07.860
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

27
00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:13.600
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1: Sports Debate.

28
00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:19.000
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

29
00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.900
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

30
00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:26.440
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

31
00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.520
You are ready to begin.

32
00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:34.700
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

33
00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.480
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

34
00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:43.120
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
